From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsDrvdata <kmsdrvdata@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:55:00 
Subject: [PATCH 0105] gpu31-kms: publish drvdata only after decon_kms_get (int62)

int60/int61 came up headless because the KMS probe installed its own
platform drvdata before calling the shim:

    ex->dev = dev;
    platform_set_drvdata(pdev, ex);     <-- struct exynos7580_device
    ...
    ex->decon = decon_kms_get(dev);     <-- reads platform_get_drvdata()
                                            and expects struct decon_device

decon_kms_get() then read a bogus decon->kms_owned out of our struct and
returned -EBUSY ("DECON already owned by the fbdev driver").  The vendor
probe was not involved: int61's vmlinux disassembly is exactly

    decon_probe:
        mov w0, #0xffffffed          // -ENODEV
        ret

and .config/autoconf had CONFIG_EXYNOS7580_DISPLAY_KMS=y, so 0103's guard was
active and the vendor never took the device.

Fix: call decon_kms_get() while the platform drvdata is still NULL (or the
vendor decon_device, as the shim expects), and install struct
exynos7580_device only after the handle is obtained, before
drm_platform_init() (->load() needs it).  On a failed hand-off the error path
still clears the drvdata, so a retry starts from NULL.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_main.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_main.c
@@ -458,7 +458,6 @@
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	ex->dev = dev;
-	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, ex);
 
 	dev_info(dev, "exynos7580: probe entry (DECON node %s), binding card0\n",
 		 of_node_full_name(dev->of_node));
@@ -486,6 +485,15 @@
 	caps = decon_kms_caps(ex->decon);
 	dev_info(dev, "exynos7580: probe: decon_kms_get ok (%u windows, default %u)\n",
 		 caps ? caps->max_win : 0, caps ? caps->default_win : 0);
+	/*
+	 * Publish our own drvdata only now.  decon_kms_get() reads
+	 * platform_get_drvdata() and expects the vendor decon_device (or
+	 * NULL): installing struct exynos7580_device before the call made it
+	 * read a bogus kms_owned and reject the hand-off with -EBUSY
+	 * ("DECON already owned by the fbdev driver").
+	 */
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, ex);
+	dev_info(dev, "exynos7580: probe: decon ok, drvdata published\n");
 
 	dev_info(dev, "exynos7580: probe: calling drm_platform_init()\n");
 	ret = drm_platform_init(&exynos7580_drm_driver, pdev);
